  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "Millions of bare circles cover this desert in a flawless grid. Spanning the Namib Desert, each mysterious barren disc is ringed by lush, tall grass.",
        "visual_query": "namib desert fairy circles aerial",
        "visual_fallback": "desert grassland aerial"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The dirt inside is completely fertile, yet any seed that sprouts there quickly dies.",
        "visual_query": "namib desert dry red soil",
        "visual_fallback": "cracked desert dirt"
      },
      {
        "narration": "How does nature build a mathematical pattern over hundreds of miles? For decades, scientists blamed subterranean termites.",
        "visual_query": "arid grassland namibia landscape",
        "visual_fallback": "dry desert savannah"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The real answer came from soil sensors. In brutal droughts, desert grasses suck water sideways, starving the center to keep their outer ring alive.",
        "visual_query": "namibia desert grass roots soil",
        "visual_fallback": "dry grass roots"
      },
      {
        "narration": "By clearing the middle, they create a natural reservoir that sustains the whole colony. But if mindless grass can self-organize this flawlessly, what else are plants secretly engineering?",
        "visual_query": "namib desert drone pattern landscape",
        "visual_fallback": "aerial desert pattern"
      }
    ],
